{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WetDepLSColumn",
    "description": "WRF-Chem's large-scale wet deposition (wetdep_ls, wetscav_onoff = -1) over one column of the EqAtmChem configuration (chem_opt = 170): every species the scheme scavenges, on one WetDepLS mount whose species axis carries all 169 of them.\n\nwetdep_ls loops over species with nothing coupling one species to another: every species sees the same column cloud-water flux and conversion factor, and they differ only in their own burden gate and their efficiency (alpha_sulf = 1 for gas-phase sulfuric acid, alpha_aerosol = 0.5 for every aerosol species, nv > numgas). WetDepLS therefore carries a species axis (NSPEC long, the first NGAS entries gases), and this document binds it to the 169 species of chem_opt 170 -- sulf, then MOSAIC's 168 aerosol species (eight sections of mass, number and water, plus ca and co3) in registry order, as WetDepColumn.c spells out -- and holds the column state once. WetDep.dc_dt = (c_out - c)/dt over [lev, spc] is the operator-split tendency a chemistry column adds to those species; the 64 other gases are untouched, and the fill script checks the dumps agree. (Until 2026-11-12 this document mounted six single-species instances, because a full-species coupling would have needed 169 generated mounts: esm has no mount-per-element, and §10.5 lifting applies to 0-D systems only. Giving the component the species axis removed the choice.)\n\nWhat the tests pin. Six steps of the separate wet-scavenging capture (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_wetscav.sh, the reference column with wetscav_onoff = -1 and cu_physics = 0, since the reference run has no wet scavenging and New Tiedtke makes all of its rain): the dry step 1300 and the event 1405-1480. Each test feeds all 169 dumped columns and asserts, against the real64 replay through chem/module_wetdep_ls.F: the activation flag of every species exactly (at the rain steps 87 of the 169 are scavenged and 82 sit under the burden gate -- those are the species that must stay unchanged, and their flags and zero removal pin it); the removal fraction of every layer and species at 1e-9 of its largest value, read from the replay as 1 - c_out/c (a fraction, so one tolerance serves species whose units span 18 orders of magnitude; no cell is floored in this capture, and the fill script refuses one that is); and the tendency over the whole [lev, spc] field at 1e-9 of its largest magnitude, which a particle number sets, so that check guards the arithmetic of the dominant species and the removal fraction guards the rest. tools/fill_wetdep_ls_column_tests.py also checks that every species that changes anywhere in a dump is on the axis.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "wet deposition",
      "chem_opt 170",
      "coupling"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Mass layers of the column, WRF kte; bound into the WetDepLS mount."
    },
    "NSPEC": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 169,
      "description": "The scavenged species of chem_opt = 170: sulf and the 168 MOSAIC aerosol species (nv > numgas)."
    },
    "NGAS": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "Gases at the head of the species axis scavenged at alpha_sulf: sulf alone for chem_opt = 170."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "WetDep": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wetdep_ls/wetdep_ls.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NLEV": "NLEV",
        "NSPEC": "NSPEC",
        "NGAS": "NGAS"
      }
    },
    "WetDepColumn": {
      "variables": {
        "qc": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Cloud-water mixing ratio, moist(:,:,:,p_qc)."
        },
        "rho": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Air density as chem_driver passes it."
        },
        "w": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Vertical velocity on the BOTTOM face of each layer, WRF w_2 as chem_driver copies it into vvel."
        },
        "ze": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Heights of the layer faces (cumulative dz8w from the ground)."
        },
        "rain": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^2",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Grid-scale rain over the step, rainncv."
        },
        "dt": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 60.0,
          "description": "The model step, grid%dt."
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev",
            "spc"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The 169 scavenged species, one column each, in their WRF chem units, on the species axis in this order: `sulf` (chem index 3) first, then the 168 aerosol species in registry order, chem indices 66-233 -- the 19 species of section 1 (so4, no3, cl, nh4, na, oin, oc, bc, hysw, water, aro1, aro2, alk1, ole1, api1, api2, lim1, lim2, num of _a01), the same 19 for sections 2-8, then ca_a01-ca_a08 and co3_a01-co3_a08."
        }
      },
      "equations": [],
